<title>USA: MBIA qualifies 10 muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies 10 muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp said Wednesday it qualified for bond insurance the following 10 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Florida $189.84 million capital outlay bonds.</p>
<p>--Clear Lake Community School District, Iowa, $6.9 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Iowa State Board of Regents, $3.8 million facilities revenue bonds</p>
<p>--Joliet, Ill., $8.345 million GO refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--Charles County, Md., $19.4 million Public Improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Utica Community Schools, Mich., $9.995 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Gorham-Middlesex Central School District, N.Y., $6.687 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Sumter County, S.C., $1.15 million GOs.</p>
<p>--De Pere, Wis., $1.025 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Greenfield, Wis., $4.115 million refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
